{
  "slug": "artist:salt-n-pepa",
  "name": "Salt-N-Pepa",
  "editorial_article": "Formed in New York City in 1985 by nursing students Cheryl James and Sandra Denton, the trio rose to prominence after their debut album, Hot, Cool & Vicious, became the first by a female rap act to achieve platinum certification. They initially operated under the name Super Nature, recording the answer record 'The Showstopper' for a class project produced by Hurby Azor. Throughout the 1990s, the group gained critical and commercial success with tracks like 'Shoop' and the En Vogue-assisted 'Whatta Man', eventually winning a 1995 Grammy for 'None of Your Business'. By challenging industry norms surrounding female sexuality in hip-hop, they secured their status as pioneering figures, leading to their 2025 induction into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame for Musical Influence.",
